# Nova first-run claim token. Optional, and strongly recommended.
#
# Cloudflare reads this file during a "Deploy to Cloudflare" and asks you for each
# value below, then stores what you type as an encrypted Worker secret.
#
# Why it matters: a freshly deployed panel has no admin password yet, and /install is
# a public page, so whoever opens it first is the one who sets the password. If you
# deploy now and finish setup later, anyone who finds the address in between can take
# the panel. Setting NOVA_CLAIM_TOKEN closes that window: the panel then refuses to
# accept a first password unless the caller presents this exact value.
#
# Generate one and keep a copy:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 16
#
# Then finish setup at:
#
#     https://<your-worker>.workers.dev/install?claim=<the value you generated>
#
# Leave it blank and the panel behaves exactly as it always has, first come first
# served, so in that case open /install and set your password immediately after the
# deploy finishes.
#
# You can never be locked out of your own panel. You own the Worker, so you can change
# or delete this value at any time in the Cloudflare dashboard, under
# Workers & Pages > your worker > Settings > Variables and Secrets. Removing it puts
# the panel back to the first-come behaviour.
#
# Note for maintainers: this belongs here rather than in wrangler.jsonc "vars".
# `wrangler deploy` reconciles the whole "vars" block from the config file on every
# deploy, so a blank var there would overwrite a real token on the next Workers Builds
# redeploy and quietly disarm the gate. Secrets are managed separately from the config
# file and survive a redeploy untouched.
NOVA_CLAIM_TOKEN=
